       <article class="topic-card panel" data-module="anatomy" data-search="anatomy physiology homeostasis structure function body systems">
        <span class="pill self-start">01 · BODY SYSTEMS</span>
        <h2 data-template-id="topic-anatomy-title" class="canva-text" style="color: rgb(56, 37, 52); font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; font-size: 24px;">Anatomy &amp; physiology</h2>
        <p data-template-id="topic-anatomy-desc" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Anatomy describes body structures; physiology explores how those structures function together.</p>
        <p data-template-id="topic-anatomy-objective" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Objective: distinguish structure from function.</p>
        <p data-template-id="topic-anatomy-terms" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Key terms: homeostasis, organ, tissue.</p>
        <p data-template-id="topic-anatomy-safety" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Safety note: normal variation exists; a diagram cannot assess an individual.</p><button type="button" class="complete-btn secondary mt-auto" data-module="anatomy" aria-label="Mark Anatomy and physiology complete"><span>Mark complete</span></button>
       </article>
       <article class="topic-card panel" data-module="pharmacology" data-search="pharmacology foundations drug dose route interaction medication">
        <span class="pill self-start">02 · MEDICINES</span>
        <h2 data-template-id="topic-pharma-title" class="canva-text" style="color: rgb(56, 37, 52); font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; font-size: 24px;">Pharmacology foundations</h2>
        <p data-template-id="topic-pharma-desc" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Pharmacology studies how medicines interact with the body, including absorption and effects.</p>
        <p data-template-id="topic-pharma-objective" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Objective: recognize why routes and interactions matter.</p>
        <p data-template-id="topic-pharma-terms" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Key terms: route, absorption, interaction.</p>
        <p data-template-id="topic-pharma-safety" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Safety note: never use study examples to choose or calculate a patient’s medication.</p><button type="button" class="complete-btn secondary mt-auto" data-module="pharmacology" aria-label="Mark Pharmacology foundations complete"><span>Mark complete</span></button>
       </article>
       <article class="topic-card panel" data-module="terminology" data-search="medical terminology prefix suffix root word">
        <span class="pill self-start">03 · LANGUAGE</span>
        <h2 data-template-id="topic-terms-title" class="canva-text" style="color: rgb(56, 37, 52); font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; font-size: 24px;">Medical terminology</h2>
        <p data-template-id="topic-terms-desc" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Word parts help students interpret unfamiliar healthcare vocabulary in context.</p>
        <p data-template-id="topic-terms-objective" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Objective: identify a prefix, root, and suffix.</p>
        <p data-template-id="topic-terms-terms" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Key terms: prefix, root, suffix.</p>
        <p data-template-id="topic-terms-safety" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Safety note: confirm the meaning of abbreviations before using them in care.</p><button type="button" class="complete-btn secondary mt-auto" data-module="terminology" aria-label="Mark Medical terminology complete"><span>Mark complete</span></button>
       </article>
       <article class="topic-card panel" data-module="infection" data-search="infection prevention hand hygiene transmission precautions">
        <span class="pill self-start">04 · PREVENTION</span>
        <h2 data-template-id="topic-infection-title" class="canva-text" style="color: rgb(56, 37, 52); font-weight: 700; font-style: normal; font-size: 24px;">Infection prevention</h2>
        <p data-template-id="topic-infection-desc" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Infection prevention uses layered practices to reduce the spread of microorganisms.</p>
        <p data-template-id="topic-infection-objective" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Objective: explain the purpose of hand hygiene.</p>
        <p data-template-id="topic-infection-terms" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Key terms: transmission, hygiene, precautions.</p>
        <p data-template-id="topic-infection-safety" class="canva-text small-copy" style="color: rgb(97, 78, 92); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-size: 16px;">Safety note: follow current local protocols and supervision in real settings.</p><button type="button" class="complete-btn secondary mt-auto" data-module="infection" aria-label="Mark Infection prevention complete"><span>Mark complete</span></button>
       </article>
       <article class="topic-card panel" data-module="vitals" data-search="vital signs temperature pulse respiration blood pressure">
        <span class="pill self-start">05 · OBSERVATION</span>
